{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (RNA-only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, while image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208). Multiprofile + avgpool clearly outperforms singleprofile and transformer aggregation. Question: Does adding image features via concatenation to the best RNA-only setup improve performance, or does the weak image signal (resnet50 alone = 0.208) degrade the strong RNA signal? Why this experiment: config_018 is the most controlled multimodal test—it holds the RNA side identical to config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) and adds only resnet50 image features with simple concat fusion. This directly isolates the marginal contribution of image features. If it beats 0.591, fusion is promising and we can explore stronger image encoders and weighted fusion; if it underperforms, we learn that resnet50 features are too weak to contribute, redirecting effort toward ViT-L or alternative fusion. This is the highest-information next step under budget constraints because it answers the fundamental 'does multimodal help?' question with minimal confounding variables."
}

